# The kitty keyboard protocol's flag 2, report event types, on the keypad
# while flag 1 is off. Without flag 1, the legacy section reports each
# keypad key as its equivalent key off the keypad. KP_1 under NumLock
# makes the text 1, so its press and its repeat send 1 and its release
# sends nothing, because events are not reported for keys that make text.
# Alt+KP_1 is Alt+1 in the legacy text keys, so its press sends ESC 1.
# KP_End without NumLock is End, which is CSI F on a press. Its repeat and
# its release carry their event types, and the modifier field is 1 when no
# modifier is held. F3 alone is SS3 R. With a modifier, or with an event
# type, F3 is CSI 13 ~, because the CSI 1 ; modifier form has no R. The
# keypad's PF3, KP_F3, is reported as F3. KP_Enter is Enter, which sends
# CR, or ESC CR with Alt, and Enter has no release events under flag 2.
# Ambiguous: the legacy section sends no event type in ESC 1, so this
# scenario reads the rule that a key event the section does not describe
# is sent as CSI u. Alt+KP_1's repeat and release are therefore CSI 49 u,
# with Alt and NumLock in the modifiers, because Alt+1 does not make text.
# Ambiguous: SS3 R has no modifier field, so F3's release takes the
# CSI 13 ; 1 : 3 ~ form. Ambiguous: KP_F3 is read as a keypad key whose
# equivalent key is F3, and the Enter note is read as covering KP_Enter.
# spec: kitty's Comprehensive keyboard handling in terminals: Report event types, Event types, Modifiers, Legacy key event encoding, Legacy functional keys, Legacy text keys, Functional key definitions
# covers: input.kitty-keyboard
size 20 2
needs key-events
send "\e[>2u"
cmd key;sym=ffb1;unicode=31;mods=32
cmd key;sym=ffb1;unicode=31;mods=32;event=repeat
cmd key;sym=ffb1;unicode=31;mods=32;event=release
cmd key;sym=ffb1;unicode=31;mods=40
cmd key;sym=ffb1;unicode=31;mods=40;event=repeat
cmd key;sym=ffb1;unicode=31;mods=40;event=release
cmd key;sym=ff9c
cmd key;sym=ff9c;event=repeat
cmd key;sym=ff9c;event=release
cmd key;sym=ff9c;mods=8
cmd key;sym=ff9c;mods=8;event=release
cmd key;sym=ffc0
cmd key;sym=ffc0;event=release
cmd key;sym=ffc0;mods=1
cmd key;sym=ffc0;mods=1;event=release
cmd key;sym=ff93;mods=1
cmd key;sym=ff93;mods=1;event=release
cmd key;sym=ff8d
cmd key;sym=ff8d;event=release
cmd key;sym=ff8d;mods=8
cmd key;sym=ff8d;mods=8;event=release
cmd key;sym=ff8d;mods=32
